WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.020
- You named him Gus,
but it's August right?

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:03.254
- It's August, yes.

00:00:03.254 --> 00:00:04.900
- So was there something
about the month of August?

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:05.750
Is that why you?

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.610
- August is when we found out
that we were having a boy.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.940
And yeah, it's also the month
that my husband was born.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.300
So we just, and we love the name Gus.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.133
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:17.000
- Yeah 'cause my husband's
last name is Goldsmith

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.300
and I like being an alliterative name.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.280
Mandy Moore.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.010
And we wanted to have a Gigi.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:23.660
- Yeah, Kelly Clarkson, River Rose.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:24.493
- Right?

00:00:24.493 --> 00:00:25.326
- Yeah. My kids are like that.

00:00:25.326 --> 00:00:26.159
I like alliteration, yeah.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:27.570
- It's fun, yeah, so easy.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:28.650
- [Kelly] It's great for monogramming.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:29.483
- Yeah.

00:00:29.483 --> 00:00:31.600
- It's also nice for that.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.310
No, but what's the hardest part you think

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:34.650
that you didn't see coming?

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.200
Like being a mama?

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.500
There's probably a lot.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.950
- I mean, I don't even know
where to begin, all of it.

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:42.280
It is every cliche in the book, right?

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.370
For those parents out there,
like life went from sepia

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:46.930
to technicolor like that.

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:49.388
I mean it's just the most overwhelming,

00:00:49.388 --> 00:00:51.500
all consuming love.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:53.200
And it's funny 'cause
I've been playing a mom

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.830
on a television show for
six years and I'm like,

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.620
wait, can we go back to the beginning now?

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.430
'Cause I know what it's like to be a mom.

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:00.930
I've been faking it.

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:02.424
- I am so method right now.

00:01:02.424 --> 00:01:03.340
- Totally.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:04.950
- In it.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.830
Was that hard though, to play a mom

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:07.677
like, not being a mom.

00:01:07.677 --> 00:01:10.800
]Cause I did hear, Milo outed
you a bit whenever he was here

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.740
'cause he said I had to teach her

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:12.980
how to do her first diaper.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:13.813
- [Mandy] Oh yeah.

00:01:13.813 --> 00:01:14.713
- [Kelly] Like change a,

00:01:14.713 --> 00:01:16.096
and you didn't know how
to do it 'cause you didn't

00:01:16.096 --> 00:01:16.929
have a kid.

00:01:16.929 --> 00:01:17.762
- I, yeah.

00:01:17.762 --> 00:01:18.915
And I just, my husband
and I, neither of us

00:01:18.915 --> 00:01:20.100
really had any experience with babies.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.300
- [Kelly] Me neither before I had one.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:25.310
- So I just remember having
to lean on Milo so hard,

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:26.830
especially in the beginning of the show.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:28.840
- Which Milo doesn't have children.

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:29.800
- [Mandy] He doesn't have children

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:31.330
but he has nieces and nephews.

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:33.850
- I have nieces and nephews and I still

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:36.450
had never changed a
diaper before my children.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:37.680
- Milo's just...

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.940
- That's your baby's butt,
take care of your own.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:43.352
I was like, I didn't make anybody do mine.

00:01:43.352 --> 00:01:45.700
- He was showing me how to
swaddle, how to change diapers.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:46.570
- He's so good at that, okay.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:47.670
- He was incredible.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.990
And even, this was like the first season.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:51.940
And then I remember
right before I gave birth

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.660
to Gus last year, same thing.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.270
It was like we were shooting
a scene where we had to

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:56.840
like, change and I'm like,

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.270
I'm about to do this in real life

00:01:58.270 --> 00:01:59.853
and I have no idea what I'm doing.

